{
  "id": "female-genital-mutilation",
  "term": "female genital mutilation",
  "definition": "Female genital mutilation is a harmful practice in which part or all of the external female genitalia is removed, or the female genital organs are otherwise injured, for non-medical reasons. It is often carried out from infancy through adolescence and is linked to serious immediate and long-term physical complications, as well as psychological problems such as depression, anxiety, post-traumatic stress, and low self-esteem.",
